From 6b6f928de108f1f931f070802d60e13799fb41fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:02:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Construct blocks from a dependency snapshot and
 ready-transaction fee heap

Keep the custom snapshot-based assembler rather than replacing it with
upstream's maintained fee-index/backlog traversal. Build a flat dependency
graph using unique direct parents, then queue each newly ready transaction
once. Select the highest individual modified-fee-rate ready transaction,
with the existing deterministic entry-ID tie break. Include parents before
children and charge only actual remaining per-transaction size/sigchecks.
Do not carry previously collected ancestor fees or fee deltas into children.

This corrects the earlier accumulator/DFS implementation: shared ancestors
were double-counted, selected parents were charged again, package-priority
reset could not occur, and already collected fees subsidized free children.
Remove those unsafe package estimates rather than claiming CPFP support.
No parent failure may release a child. No ancestry DFS or ancestor-score
updates remain. Expected complexity is O(n + m + n log n) time and
O(n + m) space, not a demonstrated speedup over modern upstream.

Native tests cover byte/sigcheck boundaries, layered diamonds, repeated
parent inputs, scarce-capacity sibling fee priority, nonfinal parents,
and existing fee-delta/free-descendant behavior. Lotus-specific adaptations
remain in subsequent consensus/compatibility patches.

Author and date are retained from the original recorded replay commit;
this corrected rationale is newly written, not recovered historical text.
Recorded-replay-commit: af72c70f4be2da3bd7cc73c0ff6e692aa5b7d49f

